curl — Complete Manual Transfer URLs, test APIs, debug TLS. Docs: curl.se , manpage , Everything curl (free book) . 0 — First Five Commands curl https://example.com # GET, print body curl -I https://example.com # HEAD: headers only (-I) curl -v https://example.com # verbose: DNS+TLS+req/resp (king of debug) curl -L https://example.com # follow redirects (-L) curl -o out.html https://example.com # save to file (-o); -O uses remote name Trio for life: -v see truth, -L follow, -sS silent but show errors. Add -w for timing (below). 1 — Options Explained (The Ones That Matter) Option Plain meaning + when -X GET/POST/PUT/DELETE Force method. GET default; POST with -d . Use --request long form in scripts. -H 'K: V' Add header. -H 'Authorization: Bearer X' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' . Repeatable. -d 'a=1&b=2' / --json '{"a":1}' Body. -d = form + POST; --json sets JSON type + POST. --data-binary @file exact bytes. -F file=@a.png / -F 'x=1' Multipart upload (forms/files). @ reads file. For pure binary PUT: -T file . -u user:pass / --netrc Basic auth. Prefer header/token; .netrc 600 beats shell history. Never -u with secrets inline on shared box. -b/-c cookies.txt Send ( -b ) / save ( -c ) cookies. -b '' enables engine without file. -e ref / -A agent Referer + User-Agent spoof for testing variants. -k / --cacert CA.pem -k skips verify (lab only!); --cacert trusts private CA properly. --cert/--key/--tlsv1.3 mTLS + version pin. Debug ciphers: --ciphers . -x proxy / --noproxy Proxy + bypass list. Env https_proxy also read. --resolve h:443:IP / --connect-to Override DNS/SNI for staging tests without /etc/hosts. -m 10 / --connect-timeout 5 --retry 3 Timeouts + retries. Always set -m in scripts or hangs forever. -sS -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code} %{time_total}
' Health-check pattern: silent, code + seconds. Full vars below. -D headers.txt / -i Dump headers to file ( -D ) or prefix body ( -i = include). 2 — Normal Usage (Daily Bread) # JSON API GET with token: curl -sS -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" https://api.example.com/notes | jq . # POST JSON: curl -sS -X POST -H 'Content-Type: application/json' -d '{"title":"hi"}' https://api.example.com/notes # form login + cookies: curl -sS -c jar.txt -d 'user=a&pass=b' https://example.com/login curl -sS -b jar.txt https://example.com/me # upload: curl -F 'file=@report.pdf' -F 'note=final' https://example.com/upload # download resume: curl -L -C - -O https://example.com/big.iso # headers/status only: curl -sSI https://example.com | head -20 3 — Testing APIs Like A Pro # pretty + fail on HTTP error: curl -sSf http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/health # timing breakdown: curl -o /dev/null -sS -w 'code:%{http_code} dns:%{time_namelookup} tls:%{time_appconnect} ttfb:%{time_starttransfer} total:%{time_total}
' https://api.example.com/ # all methods smoke test: for m in GET POST PUT DELETE; do echo -n "$m: "; curl -s -o /dev/null -w '%{http_code}
' -X $m http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/notes; done # load-ish (10 parallel): seq 1 10 | xargs -P10 -I{} curl -s -o /dev/null -w '{} %{http_code}
' http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/health # Contract: diff live vs golden JSON (keys sorted): curl -s http://127.0.0.1:3000/api/notes | jq -S . > live.json; diff golden.json live.json In CI assert http_code==200 + JSON schema ( jq -e ), not just "didn't crash". Save -D headers on failure. 4 — TLS / Auth / Proxy Debugging curl -v https://expired.badssl.com/ # see verify fail (https://badssl.com/) curl -k https://self-signed.local/ # LAB ONLY bypass curl --cacert ./myCA.pem https://internal.local/ # right way: trust CA curl --resolve api.example.com:443:10.0.0.5 https://api.example.com/ # staging IP curl -x http://127.0.0.1:8080 -k https://api.example.com/ # via Burp/ZAP (lab) curl --cert client.pem --key client.key https://mtls.local/ curl -v --tlsv1.3 https://api.example.com/ 2>&1 | grep -i -E 'cipher|TLS|cert' Secrets hygiene: prefer env vars + ~/.netrc (600) , never paste tokens in tickets. history -c after manual token test. 5 — Scripts That Don't Hang At 3am #!/bin/bash set -euo pipefail code=$(curl -sS -m 10 -o /tmp/body -w '%{http_code}' https://api.example.com/health) [[ "$code" == "200" ]] || { echo "bad $code"; cat /tmp/body; exit 1; } # config file for repeats: ~/.curlrc or -K file # -K deploy.conf: # silent=true # show-error=true # max-time=10 6 — Cheat Pairs (curl ↔ what it means) curl -I =headers? -v =why fail? -L =redirect loop? --resolve =DNS lie? -k =cert or bypass? -w time_* =slow DNS/TLS/TTFB? Pair with dig , openssl s_client -connect h:443 -servername h , tcpdump port 443 . Refs: Everything curl , man , github/curl , badssl.com (test beds) . Verbose first, assume nothing, time everything. curl never lies — servers do.
